@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam arrowColor #4b5563
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #4b5563
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #4b5563
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #4b5563
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #e5e7eb
skinparam noteBorderColor #4b5563
skinparam maxMessageSize 180
hide footbox
autonumber
title Market Desk | live import and independent reminder action

participant "Web controller" as Web
participant CatalogService as Catalog
participant "CatalogReplacement\nService" as Replace
participant "TrackingService /\nAlertService" as Tracking
participant ReminderService as Reminder
participant ShoppingService as Shopping
database "H2 repositories" as DB

== Manual live refresh: HelloController ==
[-> Web: POST /data/refresh
Web -> Catalog: refreshLive()
Catalog -> Catalog: sourceClient.fetch(); parser.parse(bytes)
alt download or validation fails
  Catalog --> Web: failure; no replacement
  [<-- Web: error; accepted data unchanged
else valid input
  Catalog -> Replace: replace(catalogue, LIVE, URL, retrievedAt, checksum)
  group One Spring transaction
    Replace -> DB: replace listings / offers; preserve product references
    Replace -> Tracking: recordLiveImport(...)
    Tracking -> DB: lock active periods; prune expired observations
    loop Each enabled exact-product / retailer period
      alt changed value or unknown transition
        Tracking -> DB: save observation and deduplication state
        Tracking -> Tracking: evaluateNewObservation(...)
        Tracking -> DB: save qualifying event + repeat state
      else unchanged value
        Tracking -> Tracking: evaluateCurrentTarget(period, price, retrievedAt, generatedAt)
        Tracking -> DB: save qualifying target + armed state; no new history
      end
    end
    Replace -> DB: save accepted-import metadata
    alt any database write fails
      note over Replace,DB
        Spring rolls back catalogue, observations and price events together.
      end note
    else all writes succeed
      note over Replace,DB: Spring commits before the caller receives success.
    end
  end
  Replace --> Catalog: ImportStatus, or propagated failure
  Catalog --> Web: accepted status, or error
  [<-- Web: show outcome after transaction completes
end
note over Replace,Tracking
  SAMPLE replacement skips tracking and live alerts.
  Unchanged values add no history; an armed target may still evaluate
  the fresh LIVE price without a retained observation.
  Unknown gaps, expired history and new periods cannot support a drop.
  Drop events snapshot both prices and their retrieval times.
end note

== Daily summary: GET /alerts or scheduler while app runs ==
Web -> Tracking: AlertService.processDue(now)
Tracking -> DB: store at most one eligible summary per Hong Kong date
note over Tracking,DB
  Include unread, unsummarized, currently eligible price events.
  Quiet hours and snooze delay availability.
  A catch-up summary uses its actual generation time.
end note

== Explicit reminder action: ReminderController ==
[-> Web: POST /reminders/{id}/add
Web -> Reminder: addToList(id), with no outer transaction
Reminder -> DB: read product, quantity and saved retailer choice
Reminder -> Shopping: add(productCode, quantity, selectedRetailerCode)
Shopping -> DB: validate / merge item in its own mutation transaction
alt quantity / retailer conflict / unavailable product
  Shopping --> Reminder: validation error; no list change
  Reminder --> Web: error
else valid request
  DB --> Shopping: list change commits
  Shopping --> Reminder: success
  Reminder --> Web: success
end
[<-- Web: show outcome; reminder due state is unchanged
note over Reminder,Shopping
  Quiet hours do not block a manual add.
  Only clear / snooze changes the reminder schedule.
end note

legend bottom left
  Grouped Tracking / Alert lifeline represents two actual services.
  CatalogService delegates input to ConsumerCouncilSourceClient and CatalogJsonParser.
  NotificationScheduler is the alternative caller for the daily summary check.
  Retrieval time and alert generation time differ; source price date is unknown.
  A closed app collects no prices and delivers no notifications.
endlegend
@enduml
